<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8356"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nm_pi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nm_pi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 8:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->could it be that &#34;BTK&#34; is an experiment by internal or external groups to determine what type of control can be exerted on LE and American Society through this type of terror??? Recall, the 70s were a period of significant international terrorism. Just a thought...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8356-->
<!--Post: 8373--><!--Time: 1109097529-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8373"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 10:38 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Possibly, but most terrorist groups tend to be bloodier. I think, however, if there were even a hint of actual &#40;foriegn&#41; terrorist activity in the area, people would forget about BTK in a heartbeat. <BR> <BR>Compare the body count from BTK over 30 years, including all of the suspected victims, with a single car bombing and there isn,t much difference. <BR> <BR>The attention BTK receives is really as much about morbid facination as fear.  <BR> <BR>Whereas a terrorist attack is perceived as a true attack on our society...BTK is perceived as a &#34;brain derailment&#34; &#40;pun intended&#41;. He is just &#34;one of those things that is going to happen occasionally&#34;, and you deal with it the best you can.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8373-->
<!--Post: 8427--><!--Time: 1109122442-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8427"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 5:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Then, again...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8427-->
<!--Post: 8447--><!--Time: 1109134484-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8447"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 8:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think you have cracked the case. Let me call Elvis and let him know!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8447-->
<!--Post: 8450--><!--Time: 1109136152-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8450"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 9:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Only the North Koreans could come up with a plan as goofy as &#34;Operation BTK&#34;.  Right up there with their &#34;Beach Blanket Abduction&#34; operations.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8450-->
<!--Post: 8768--><!--Time: 1109316991-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8768"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 11:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is a good point to mention something. Some months ago, I started a thread called, &#34;Is BTK a terrorist?&#34; I mentioned the new laws since the 9/11 attack, and that maybe use of the US mails as well as the Internet was subject to closer legal scrutiny than before and could be used against BTK, were he to be declared a terrorist. That&#39;s about the only chance, IMO, he&#39;ll be caught; unless every agency in this investigation shares <b>everything</b> with each other - and they aren&#39;t going to share - I see things as bleak. <BR> <BR>I wrote all of this on the chance that BTK reads these boards and I was basically trying to <u>scare BTK</u> more than anything else, let alone the ensuing, brief fuss on that thread if the thread even still exists - I haven&#39;t checked. <BR> <BR>Okay, a little grandiose on my part with that idea I guess but BTK does read these boards and half my posts are written with this in mind. I don&#39;t believe BTK only reads the &#34;To BTK&#34; thread. But I guess one never knows.  <BR> <BR>On BTK as terrorist; by definition, he may be considered one. The FBI has made it clear they won&#39;t be pursuing BTK as a terrorist or as much of anything else. Yet again, ego concern of who gets the glory if BTK is snagged seems to have caused a rift. On this one I&#39;ll give WPD the benefit of the doubt, based solely on the FBI&#39;s abysmal record of stealing credit when succeeding and casting blame right back at the locals when an operation fails.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8768-->
<!--Post: 10661--><!--Time: 1110093749-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10661"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 05, 2005 - 11:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You know if the CIA would put a spy satelite in a geosyncronized orbit over Tora Bora, and had a web page to show each photo as it downloaded with some ultra-zoom viewing software, we could sit up all night looking for Osama. And if it should, say stray over a nude beach on the Riviera occasionally, that would be okay too.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
